# 🔍 YOLO Object Detection Web App

### Upload any image — get real-time object detection powered by YOLOv8 Nano, served through a Flask REST API with a sleek dark-theme UI.

</div>

---

## ✨ Features

- 🖼️ Drag & drop image upload
- 🤖 Real-time inference using a locally trained **YOLOv8n model**
- 📦 Annotated output with **color-coded bounding boxes**
- 📊 Detection table — object name, confidence %, and coordinates
- ⚡ Live stats: total objects, avg confidence, top detection class

---

## 🗂️ Project Structure

```
yolo-object-detection/
│
├── 📁 runs/              # YOLOv8 training runs & results
├── 📁 static/            # CSS, JS, assets
├── 📁 templates/         # Flask HTML templates
│
├── 🐍 api.py             # Main Flask app — run this!
├── 🧠 best.pt            # Custom trained model weights
├── 🧠 yolov8n.pt         # Base YOLOv8 Nano weights
├── 🐍 test.py            # Standalone test script
├── 🖼️  test_image.jpg    # Sample test image
└── 🖼️  bus.jpg           # COCO sample image
```

---

## ⚡ Quick Start

```bash
# 1. Clone the repo
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/yolo-object-detection-webapp.git
cd yolo-object-detection-webapp

# 2. Install dependencies
pip install ultralytics flask pillow numpy opencv-python

# 3. Run the app
python api.py
```

Then open **`http://localhost:5000`** in your browser.

---

## 🔌 API Endpoint

**`POST /detect`** — multipart/form-data (image file)

```json
{
  "detections": [
    { "object": "person", "confidence": 90.3, "bounding_box": [140.14, 35.69, 437.68, 313.03] }
  ],
  "total_objects": 13,
  "avg_confidence": 59.4,
  "top_detection": "person"
}
```

